      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogies. Let me focus on providing you with practical advice.\n\nWhen I said \"goblin trap,\" I was referring to the possibility of hidden fees or complications that might arise when booking a flight. For example, some airlines might charge extra for things like checked bags or seat selection, which could add up quickly.\n\nAs for \"goblin's lair,\" I was using it to describe a long, complicated route with multiple layovers. You want to avoid routes that involve a lot of backtracking or waiting around, as they can be time-consuming and frustrating.\n\nTo minimize travel time, I recommend focusing on flights with shorter layovers, ideally under 2 hours. You can also try to find flights that depart early in the morning or late at night, when there are fewer passengers and less congestion in the air.\n\nIn terms of specific routes, I'd be happy to help you explore options. Can you tell me a bit more about your travel plans and preferences? What's your budget like, and do you have any specific destinations or airlines in mind?",
